Z||000004||HotFieroGT||10-20-1999||12:09 AM||||I suspect it is one of two things, either somebody somehow put the clutch disk in backwards or the slave cylinder isn't working right.  It had a bunch of new parts (slave cylinder, clutch lever, etc.) It kind of looks like somebody was trying to fix it but didn't know what they were doing.  I bought It from a wholesaler in Downey, CA who just wanted to get rid of it, lucky for me!  Haven't had a chance to dig into it yet.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Boxdin||10-20-1999||02:32 PM||||After repairing 3 cars with this problem among others, it seems like the fuild used in these clutch sys is very prone to rust , or the line is or? You'll be amazed at how much crud and rust comes out of the clutch line. ||||reg||1
